        "# CNC Image Creator\n\n**Stage 1** runs on its own. **Stage 2 starts muted.**\n\n## How to use\n1. Run. Look at the **Stage 1** image.\n2. Not happy? Run again (seed is on `randomize`).\n3. Happy? Set the Stage 1 **Random Noise** `control_after_generate` to **`fixed`**. This locks the seed so Stage 1 reproduces the *same* image instead of a new one.\n4. Select the **STAGE 2** group by its title bar and press **Ctrl+M** to unmute it.\n5. Edit the Stage 2 prompt to describe the change you want, then Run.\n\nStage 1 will not recompute - ComfyUI caches it once the seed is fixed - so Stage 2 refines the exact image you approved.\n\nTo go back to generating new images: Ctrl+M the STAGE 2 group again and set `control_after_generate` back to `randomize`.\n\n## Note on img2img in FLUX.2\nThere is no denoise slider. Klein edits via **reference latent conditioning** - the source image is VAE-encoded and attached to both the positive and negative conditioning. Strength is controlled by how you word the prompt: say what to keep as well as what to change.\n\n---\n\n## Saving is OFF by default\n\nEvery image lands in a **Preview Image** node. Nothing is written to `ComfyUI/output` unless you deliberately save it.\n\n### To keep an image\n1. Set the sampler's `control_after_generate` to **`fixed`** (locks the seed).\n2. Type a descriptive name into the **Save Image** node's `filename_prefix` - replace `RENAME_BEFORE_SAVING`.\n3. Select the **Save Image** node and press **Ctrl+M** to unmute it.\n4. Run. The seed is locked so nothing regenerates - ComfyUI serves the cached image and just writes the file.\n5. **Ctrl+M it back to muted** before your next exploration round.\n\nThe Save Image nodes sit *outside* the coloured groups on purpose, so muting or unmuting a stage never switches saving on behind your back.\n\n### Naming\n`subject_pose_variant` - e.g. `raven_sideprofile_flatbg_A`, `skull_frontal_deepcut_B`. No spaces. The name follows the file all the way to the STL and the g-code, so make it mean something."
      ],
